flowchart TB
  accTitle: Three AI Coding Interaction Modes
  accDescr: The tutorial illustrates editor completions with GitHub Copilot, IDE conversations with Cursor, and a terminal agent with Claude Code. These modes serve different parts of a workflow; this diagram does not rank products or define their capability limits.
  modes["Understand three modes<br/>by where work begins"]
  subgraph copilot["GitHub Copilot · Editor completions"]
    direction TB
    edit["Write code<br/>in the editor"]
    suggest["Read inline suggestions<br/>as you type"]
    accept["Accept or adapt a suggestion<br/>and keep editing"]
    edit --> suggest --> accept
  end
  subgraph cursor["Cursor · IDE conversations"]
    direction TB
    project["Open a project<br/>and ask about the code"]
    chat["Discuss implementation<br/>inside the IDE"]
    iterate["Inspect the changes<br/>and iterate in conversation"]
    project --> chat --> iterate
  end
  subgraph claude["Claude Code · Terminal agent"]
    direction TB
    task["Describe a terminal task<br/>claude"]
    context["Use repository context<br/>and MCP tools as needed"]
    execute["Edit across files<br/>and run commands and tests"]
    task --> context --> execute
  end
  modes --> copilot
  modes --> cursor
  modes --> claude
